.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@eslint/eslintrc Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "ESLintRC Library"
.PP
This repository contains the legacy ESLintRC configuration file format for ESLint\&. This package is not intended for use outside of the ESLint ecosystem\&. It is ESLint-specific and not intended for use in other programs\&.

.PP
\fBNote:\fP This package is frozen except for critical bug fixes as ESLint moves to a new config system\&.
.SH "Installation"
.PP
You can install the package as follows:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @eslint/eslintrc \-D
# or
yarn add @eslint/eslintrc \-D
# or
pnpm install @eslint/eslintrc \-D
# or
bun install @eslint/eslintrc \-D
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage (ESM)"
.PP
The primary class in this package is \fRFlatCompat\fP, which is a utility to translate ESLintRC-style configs into flat configs\&. Here's how you use it inside of your \fReslint\&.config\&.js\fP file:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { FlatCompat } from "@eslint/eslintrc";
import js from "@eslint/js";
import path from "path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "url";

// mimic CommonJS variables \-\- not needed if using CommonJS
const __filename = fileURLToPath(import\&.meta\&.url);
const __dirname = path\&.dirname(__filename);

const compat = new FlatCompat({
    baseDirectory: __dirname,                  // optional; default: process\&.cwd()
    resolvePluginsRelativeTo: __dirname,       // optional
    recommendedConfig: js\&.configs\&.recommended, // optional unless you're using "eslint:recommended"
    allConfig: js\&.configs\&.all,                 // optional unless you're using "eslint:all"
});

export default [

    // mimic ESLintRC\-style extends
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.extends("standard", "example", "plugin:react/recommended"),

    // mimic environments
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.env({
        es2020: true,
        node: true
    }),

    // mimic plugins
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.plugins("jsx\-a11y", "react"),

    // translate an entire config
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.config({
        plugins: ["jsx\-a11y", "react"],
        extends: "standard",
        env: {
            es2020: true,
            node: true
        },
        rules: {
            semi: "error"
        }
    })
];
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage (CommonJS)"
.PP
Using \fRFlatCompat\fP in CommonJS files is similar to ESM, but you'll use \fRrequire()\fP and \fRmodule\&.exports\fP instead of \fRimport\fP and \fRexport\fP\&. Here's how you use it inside of your \fReslint\&.config\&.js\fP CommonJS file:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const { FlatCompat } = require("@eslint/eslintrc");
const js = require("@eslint/js");

const compat = new FlatCompat({
    baseDirectory: __dirname,                  // optional; default: process\&.cwd()
    resolvePluginsRelativeTo: __dirname,       // optional
    recommendedConfig: js\&.configs\&.recommended, // optional unless using "eslint:recommended"
    allConfig: js\&.configs\&.all,                 // optional unless using "eslint:all"
});

module\&.exports = [

    // mimic ESLintRC\-style extends
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.extends("standard", "example", "plugin:react/recommended"),

    // mimic environments
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.env({
        es2020: true,
        node: true
    }),

    // mimic plugins
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.plugins("jsx\-a11y", "react"),

    // translate an entire config
    \&.\&.\&.compat\&.config({
        plugins: ["jsx\-a11y", "react"],
        extends: "standard",
        env: {
            es2020: true,
            node: true
        },
        rules: {
            semi: "error"
        }
    })
];
.fi
.PP
.SH "Troubleshooting"
.PP
\fBTypeError: Missing parameter 'recommendedConfig' in FlatCompat constructor\fP

.PP
The \fRrecommendedConfig\fP option is required when any config uses \fReslint:recommended\fP, including any config in an \fRextends\fP clause\&. To fix this, follow the example above using \fR@eslint/js\fP to provide the \fReslint:recommended\fP config\&.

.PP
\fBTypeError: Missing parameter 'allConfig' in FlatCompat constructor\fP

.PP
The \fRallConfig\fP option is required when any config uses \fReslint:all\fP, including any config in an \fRextends\fP clause\&. To fix this, follow the example above using \fR@eslint/js\fP to provide the \fReslint:all\fP config\&.
